@startuml host-local-model
title AI Sandbox - Host-Local Model DFD
caption DFD3 level 1 diagram of optional llama.cpp inference from the VM.

left to right direction
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam ArrowColor black
hide stereotype
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor white
  BorderColor black
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor white
  BorderColor black
}
skinparam rectangle<<process>> {
  RoundCorner 25
}
skinparam rectangle<<trust-boundary>> {
  BorderStyle dashed
  BackgroundColor transparent
}

rectangle "E1\nDeveloper / operator" as E1
rectangle "E2\nLAN clients\n(only if broadly bound)" as E2

rectangle "TB1  Host machine" as TB1 <<trust-boundary>> {
  rectangle "P1\nUTM / vmnet bridge" as P1 <<process>>
  rectangle "P2\nllama.cpp server\n192.168.64.1:8080" as P2 <<process>>
  database "D1\nGGUF model file" as D1
  database "D2\nMultimodal projection file" as D2
  database "D3\nHost memory / model context" as D3

  rectangle "TB2  NixOS guest VM" as TB2 <<trust-boundary>> {
    rectangle "P3\nOpenCode" as P3 <<process>>
    rectangle "P4\nGuest network stack" as P4 <<process>>
    database "D4\nOpenCode configuration\nbaseURL and model limits" as D4
    database "D5\nProject workspace and context" as D5
  }
}

E1 <--> P3 : F1  Prompts and model responses
D4 --> P3 : F2  Provider URL, model name,\nand context/output limits
P3 <--> D5 : F3  Context reads and source changes

P3 <--> P4 : F4  OpenAI-compatible API traffic\nHTTP
P4 <--> P1 : F5  UTM Shared Network\n192.168.64.0/24
P1 <--> P2 : F6  Inference requests and responses\nHTTP, port 8080

D1 --> P2 : F7  Model weights
D2 --> P2 : F8  Projection data
P2 <--> D3 : F9  Loaded weights, KV cache,\nand inference state

E2 <--> P2 : F10  Inference API traffic\npossible only with LAN-reachable binding

@enduml
